[00:36.88]M: Have you decided what you wish to study?
[00:39.58]W: Yes, professor.
[00:40.66]W: I wish to study architecture.
[00:43.00]M: Ah, that's a wonderful profession.
[00:45.50]M: Why did you choose it?
[00:46.94]W: I gave a lot of thought to things you said during our last discussion.
[00:50.36]W: And I decided architecture made the most sense for me.
[00:54.18]W: In particular, I'm attracted to the marriage of design and engineering.
[00:59.36]M: That's great, but I seem to remember you were preoccupied with all the lofty mathematics.
[01:05.48]M: You no longer think this aspect will be too hard for you?
[01:08.62]W: No. I was doing some online research and I think I should be able to manage.
[01:14.40]W: Math might be the toughest subject I encounter in the curriculum, but I'll simply put in the work required.
[01:20.94]W: I'm certain the fruits of my labor will pay off.
[01:23.42]M: I'm sure that's true.
[01:25.88]M: Due to its material nature, architecture is one field where you will be able to clearly witness the contribution you make to a city.
[01:34.00]M: And the legacies you build will last much longer than any of us mortals.
[01:38.54]W: Yeah, I guess that's true too.
[01:41.02]W: So what subjects do you think I should start brushing up on in preparation?
[01:45.62]W: I have the whole summer.
[01:46.78]M: These days, architecture is a very diverse and dynamic degree.
[01:52.64]M: Most universities will encourage you to learn different things from fields as wide-ranging as philosophy and economics.
[02:00.66]M: Nevertheless, I would suggest you start with computer science, because there will be many intricate visuals you will have to produce as part of your projects.
[02:10.70]W: Any software in particular you think I should start with?
[02:14.12]M: Photoshop is a good place.
[02:15.42]M: If you aren't yet, try to become as proficient as you can with it.
[02:21.08]M: And another thing that I would recommend you learn as much as you can is fine arts, in particular, the history of Western art.
[02:37.38]Q1. Why does the woman wish to study architecture?
[02:55.66]Q2. How does the woman say she will overcome the difficulty in learning mathematics?
[03:15.34]Q3. What does the man say about architects' contribution to a city?
[03:34.96]Q4. What subject does the man suggest the woman start with?
[03:54.24]W: So, as I mentioned over the phone, we are looking for someone who is very discreet.
[03:59.02]W: I can't stress this enough.
[04:00.74]M: I fully understand.
[04:02.70]W: As we all know, being such a famous football player at Real Madrid, Mr Sanchez has a very high public profile.
[04:10.26]W: This means he cannot leave the house without being recognized and harassed.
[04:14.96]M: Yes, I completely understand how imperative it would be to respect Mr Sanchez's private life.
[04:22.28]W: Good.
[04:22.94]W: As his personal assistant, you would be required to run common everyday chores for Mr Sanchez, things he cannot do himself due to his fame, like going to the supermarket or post office.
[04:34.62]W: So, well, at first sight it may appear that working for a celebrity is very glamorous.
[04:40.50]W: Nothing could be further from the truth.
[04:42.76]W: I'm telling you this so that you don't get any false expectations of what the job has to offer you.
[04:48.32]M: Thanks.
[04:49.10]M: I understand this too.
[04:50.82]M: This is my first job after graduating from university.
[04:53.78]M: So frankly, I don't have much prior working experience.
[04:58.54]M: I am, however, very excited about the prospect of joining this company and very keen to start from the bottom in whatever capacity I may be of use.
[05:08.12]W: That's good to hear.
[05:09.24]W: You sound very energetic.
[05:11.00]W: Tell me why do you think you are well suited for this job?
[05:15.14]M: Well, firstly, I love football.
[05:17.10]M: I'm a lifelong Real Madrid supporter and go to their games every weekend I can.
[05:22.74]M: I would simply love to have a job where I'm involved in some capacity with Real Madrid, regardless of the position and salary.
[05:31.66]M: And secondly, I think what this company does in sports consultancy is very cool.
[05:37.42]M: And I think my language skills could prove very useful down the road.
[05:42.70]W: Please tell me more about your language skills.
[05:45.16]M: I am fully fluent in English and Spanish and have a working proficiency in French.
